# .env.example
# Copy this to .env for local development. Never commit .env or .env.production —
# .gitignore already guards this; don't defeat it.
#
# Variable names must match src/shared/config/env.ts, src/shared/config/env.d.ts and
# src/shared/lib/supabaseClient.ts exactly. No VITE_ prefix — this is React Native,
# not Vite. Real per-environment injection into the RN bundle (EAS environment
# variables per build profile) is P0-5.0's job; until that lands these are read via
# `process.env` for local dev only, which means THEY ARE BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE AT
# BUILD TIME and are identical for every environment. That is the reason P0-5.0
# exists — see the production gate below.
#
# The URL below is not secret (it ships inside the compiled app either way).
# The anon key IS environment-specific and goes in your local .env only —
# never hardcode it, never commit it. Get it from Project Settings → API in
# the Supabase dashboard for the project you're pointing at.
#
# NEVER put the service-role key here or anywhere client-side. It bypasses
# every RLS policy in supabase/migrations/**. It belongs in Edge Function /
# CI secrets only (P0-3.0 §5.4, P0-5.0).

# ── DEV (bluesmoke-dev — default for local app development) ─────────────────
SUPABASE_URL=https://hejwrhijrztgdysycvto.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-dev-anon-key

# ── Persona — age verification (P2-1.0, spec §6) ─────────────────────────────
# 🔴 PRODUCTION GATE (OQ-11). `PERSONA_ENVIRONMENT` may be `production` ONLY after
# ALL of the following are in writing:
#   1. Client acceptance that ID images leave the device to a third-party vendor
#   2. A signed DPA with Persona
#   3. An agreed owner for the per-verification cost (absent from the fixed-price PRD)
#   4. A vendor-side erasure path for GDPR/CCPA subject requests
# Until then this stays `sandbox`, which processes TEST DOCUMENTS ONLY — no real
# person's ID is transmitted. The account is currently developer-owned and must be
# moved to an org-owned account before any production traffic.
#
# 🔴 PERSONA_TEMPLATE_ID IS AN AGE-GATE CONTROL, NOT A CONVENIENCE SETTING — spec §6.6 item 3.
# `persona-webhook` refuses to set `age_verified = true` for any inquiry whose template is not
# this exact id (`_shared/inquiryTemplate.ts`). So this value is the single place that decides
# which Persona configuration is trusted to answer "is this person 18+".
#
# Before changing it, the new template MUST be opened in the Persona dashboard and its age
# requirement confirmed to be 18 — Inquiries → Templates → the template → Flow → the government
# ID verification step. The template's NAME is not evidence; the configured check is.
# A wrong id here fails CLOSED (nobody is verified, logged as `template_not_confirmed`), which
# is loud and safe — unlike the pre-2026-08-09 state, where there was no check at all and an
# identity-only template would have opened the gate for anyone with a valid ID, at any age.
#
# ⚠️ The value below is "Government ID (with autoclassification) and Selfie" — an IDENTITY-only
# template that carries NO age requirement. It must be replaced with the confirmed
# age-verifying template id before verification can pass. Tracked as min_age / OQ-11.
#
# ── Runbook: changing PERSONA_TEMPLATE_ID ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# This variable lives in TWO places and they must not diverge. The app inlines it at BUNDLE
# time from this file (babel.config.js → transform-inline-environment-variables); the
# `persona-webhook` Edge Function reads it at RUNTIME from Supabase Edge Function secrets.
# Update one and not the other and the app opens inquiries against template A while the webhook
# only trusts template B — every verification then fails closed as `mismatch`, which looks
# exactly like a total outage.
#   1. Persona dashboard → Inquiries → Templates → the template → Flow → the government-ID
#      verification step. Confirm the age requirement is 18. Screenshot it (the evidence
#      min_age has been asking for). The template's NAME is not evidence.
#   2. Copy the FULL template id. The dashboard table truncates it (itmpl_AW8e9aVuRLU…) and a
#      truncated value will not prefix-match — it fails closed, correctly but confusingly.
#   3. Update this file / your .env  → the app.
#   4. Update the Edge Function secret → the webhook.  (`supabase secrets set`)
#   5. REBUILD the app. A Metro restart is not enough; the value is inlined at bundle time.
#      Use --reset-cache.
#   6. Run one sandbox inquiry end to end and confirm the webhook applied it, rather than
#      logging `template_not_confirmed`.
PERSONA_TEMPLATE_ID=itmpl_AW8e9aVphL2MHDmHsLFKScZsHNLPUA
PERSONA_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# ── STAGING (bluesmoke-staging) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL=https://rwhawlvigzakmjwpzvnc.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-staging-anon-key

# ── PRODUCTION (bluesmoke-prod — does not exist yet) ─────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-prod-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-prod-anon-key
